          "id": "paradigm",
          "label": "Paradigm",
          "startSec": 0,
          "endSec": 42.76090909090909,
          "text": "Since the dawn of computing, programming has always meant the same thing: anticipate every scenario and write code for it. If you miss a case, the program breaks. But tool‑using agents flip the script. Instead of explicitly handling every possible scenario, you depend on AI models to make decisions and take action for you. In this new kind of programming, first you start with an agent—a language model. Then you give it a tool. And then you assign it a procedure to follow. And then you put guardrails around that to guide it toward the goal. This is a completely new way to automate work with computers. A new kind of computer program.",
