      "cues": [
        {
          "id": "graphs",
          "label": "No Graphs Required",
          "startSec": 189.3381818181819,
          "endSec": 214.629090909091,
          "text": "In most programming languages, if you want execution that can pause and resume like this, you're forced into something like a graph workflow, where you have to write code that's structured around nodes, edges, and conditional edges. With Tactus, it's transparent. You write normal code, and the runtime handles pausing and resuming behind the scenes. The graph nodes are still there, but you don't have to think about them.",
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "pause",
              "startSec": 189.3381818181819,
              "endSec": 189.5381818181819,
              "durationSec": 0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "tts",
              "startSec": 189.5381818181819,
              "endSec": 214.629090909091,
              "text": "In most programming languages, if you want execution that can pause and resume like this, you're forced into something like a graph workflow, where you have to write code that's structured around nodes, edges, and conditional edges. With Tactus, it's transparent. You write normal code, and the runtime handles pausing and resuming behind the scenes. The graph nodes are still there, but you don't have to think about them."
            }
          ],
          "bullets": []
        }
